<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates steady to softer.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were softer from one week to one month, while the rest were steady, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>Banks expected short-term rates to drop further because of the high liquidity in the system, they said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR rates had been on a decline in recent days due to the positive news of a low 4.6 percent inflation on Monday and the inflow of foreign funds.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  MAY 9		 MAY 8</p>
<p>    1 W		10  1/8		 10  1/4</p>
<p>    2 W		10  1/16		10  3/16</p>
<p>    1 M		9 15/16		 10</p>
<p>    2 M		10  1/16		10  1/16</p>
<p>    3 M		10  1/8		 10  1/8</p>
<p>    6 M		10  7/16		10  7/16</p>
<p>    12M		10 11/16		10 11/16</p>
<p>    VAL		13-May		  9-May</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (63 2) 841-8937 Fax 817-6267</p>
